## Context

Vietnam has major inventory coverage gaps. Start with the saved principal official RMP inventories, retaining the distinction between named projects, plans and unnamed disclosure slots.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

An official inventory row lacks a project page, another maps to an existing ID and one describes an unnamed count. All receive explicit dispositions; the count creates no fabricated named project or financing event.

## Actions

Inventory all relevant saved official RMP tables and their boundaries; ingest source rows as positions/membership with row locators. Classify existing events, implementation rows, source claims, plan rows and VNM pilot observations without invented transition dates. Review joins and one-to-many crosswalks. Preserve unknowns, cancelled/nonselected observations and search history. Produce candidate website differences and a migration/writer-transfer report; leave publication legacy until accepted.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every selected official inventory row and VNM legacy row has a traceable disposition
- [ ] Legacy IDs/routes and source wording survive; any count change is explained
- [ ] Positions/cutoffs never become unsupported event dates or payments
- [ ] Candidate VNM export works beside all three unchanged country views
- [ ] Importer and crosswalk conventions are reusable for the next countries

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

